The Laplace-domain equivalent of an inductor with initial current \(i(0^-)\) is \[V(s)
=
sLI(s)-Li(0^-)\] or equivalently, an impedance \(sL\) in series with a voltage source of magnitude \(Li(0^-)\). <img src="img/b88c87b4360eedd3.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,320px)"> Comparing the given circuit with the standard Laplace equivalent, \(sL=0.002s\) Hence, \[L=0.002~\text{H}
=2~\text{mH}\] Also, the series voltage source is \[Li(0^-)=1~\text{mV}
=10^{-3}~\text{V}\] Therefore, \[i(0^-)
=
\frac{10^{-3}}{2\times10^{-3}}
=
0.5~\text{A}\] Hence, the correct answer is \[\boxed{\textbf{A. }0.5~\text{A}}\]

